# WA Mining Operations Dashboard – Git Ignore Rules
# ------------------------------------------------

# Dataset CSVs are deliberately NOT ignored.
#
# Both DATABASES/raw/Major_Resource_Projects.csv and
# DATABASES/Cleaned_Mining_Data/Major_Resource_Projects_Cleaned.csv are
# tracked on purpose: the raw file is the input SQL/01's \copy step reads,
# and the cleaned file is what backend/app/db/seed.py loads, so a fresh
# clone can run the pipeline and seed the app without downloading
# anything. DATABASES/README_database.md documents both.
#
# An earlier "DATABASES/raw/*.csv" rule here said the opposite ("too
# large, downloadable from source") and had no effect on the already-
# tracked file, but it did mean a *newly* dropped raw CSV would be
# invisible to git -- directly contradicting that same README's refresh
# procedure, step 4 of which is "replace raw/Major_Resource_Projects.csv".
# Removed rather than reworded.

# OS generated files
.DS_Store

# Backend (FastAPI)
backend/.venv/
backend/__pycache__/
backend/**/__pycache__/
backend/.env

# Frontend (React + Vite)
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
frontend/.env
frontend/*.tsbuildinfo

# Root (Netlify Functions + Drizzle + Netlify Database)
node_modules/
deno.lock

# Netlify CLI local runtime state (created by `netlify dev`)
.netlify/state.json
.netlify/functions-serve/
.netlify/functions-internal/
.netlify/blobs-serve/
.netlify/db/
.netlify/v1/

